/*
time complexity - o(1) for each operation 
space complexity - O(n) 
INTUITION
What problem are we solving?

We want a cache that:

Returns values in O(1) time

Evicts the Least Recently Used item when full

So we combine:

HashMap → fast lookup

Doubly Linked List → fast remove + reorder

2️⃣ How is “recent usage” tracked?

The right end of the list = most recently used

The left end of the list = least recently used

Two dummy nodes (left, right) simplify edge cases

left <-> LRU ... MRU <-> right

3️⃣ What does insert(node) do?

Inserts the node just before right

Meaning: “this key was just used”

👉 Always moves nodes to MRU position

4️⃣ What does remove(node) do?

Detaches a node from the list in O(1)

Used when:

Accessing a key (to move it)

Updating a key

Evicting LRU

5️⃣ get(key) logic

If key doesn’t exist → return -1

If it exists:

Remove it from its current position

Insert it at the MRU end

Return its value

👉 Reading a key counts as “recently used”

6️⃣ put(key, value) logic

If key already exists:

Remove old node (to avoid duplicates)

Create new node and insert at MRU end

If cache exceeds capacity:

Evict left.next (the LRU node)

Remove it from both list and hashmap
*/
class Node{
    Node prev;
    Node next;
    int key;
    int val;
    public Node(int key,int val){
        this.key = key;
        this.val = val;
        this.prev = null;
        this.next = null;
    }
}
class LRUCache {
    int size;
    HashMap<Integer,Node> cache;
    Node left;
    Node right;
    public LRUCache(int capacity) {
        this.size = capacity;
        this.cache = new HashMap<>();
        this.left = new Node(0,0);
        this.right = new Node(0,0);
        this.left.next = this.right;
        this.right.prev = this.left;
    }
    public void insert(Node node){
        Node prev = this.right.prev;
        prev.next = node;
        node.prev = prev;
        node.next = this.right;
        this.right.prev = node;

    }
    public void remove(Node node){
        Node prev = node.prev;
        Node next = node.next;
        prev.next = next;
        next.prev = prev;
    }
    
    public int get(int key) {
        if(cache.containsKey(key)){
            Node cur = cache.get(key);
            remove(cur);
            insert(cur);
            return cur.val;
        }
        return -1;
    }
    
    public void put(int key, int value) {
        if(cache.containsKey(key)){
            remove(cache.get(key));
        }
        Node curNode = new Node(key,value);
        cache.put(key,curNode);
        insert(curNode);
        if(cache.size() > size){
            Node lru = this.left.next;
            remove(lru);
            cache.remove(lru.key);
        }

    }
}
